ory of Tolerance)","Artist":"Franz Anton Maulbertsch","Date":"1785","Medium":"etching on laid paper","CreditLine":"Ruth and Jacob Kainen Memorial Acquisition Fund","URL":"https://www.nga.gov/artworks/221103","ImageURL":"https://api.nga.gov/iiif/68c6b76f-04ba-413a-8c24-d94393f728ab/full/!800,800/0/default.jpg"},{"ObjectID":226503,"Title":"Plate 28. Coal Beds of Bear River","Artist":"Andrew Joseph Russell","Date":"1869","Medium":"albumen silver print","CreditLine":"Avalon Fund and New Century Fund","URL":"https://www.nga.gov/artworks/226503","ImageURL":"https://api.nga.gov/iiif/85ab5efb-efb5-4797-8cc7-c853e2aeaa09/full/!800,800/0/default.jpg"},{"ObjectID":227043,"Title":"Portrait of a Man","Artist":"Augustus Washington","Date":"c. 1845","Medium":"daguerreotype","CreditLine":"Ross J. Kelbaugh Collection, Purchased with support from the Ford Foundation","URL":"https://www.nga.gov/artworks/227043","ImageURL":"https://api.nga.gov/iiif/49f407f1-e621-4fab-9a2a-49474d5a313d/full/!800,800/0/default.jpg"},{"ObjectID":228123,"Title":"Das Infernalische Abendmahl (The Infernal Last Supper) (in-text plate) from mock-up of Georg Heym: Umbra Vitae (Georg Heym: Shadow of Life)","Artist":"Ernst Ludwig Kirchner","Date":"1912/1922","Medium":"woodcut from a bound volume with 51 woodcuts (including cover and front and back endpapers) on wove paper","CreditLine":"Gift of Ruth Cole Kainen","URL":"https://www.nga.gov/artworks/228123","ImageURL":"https://api.nga.gov/iiif/96059a7c-f9d6-411a-bf3c-487b91aac265/full/!800,800/0/default.jpg"}]